A||||35||ChadMan||Drove a Del Sol Si||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||08-08-2001||02:03 PM||||I was driving home and saw a 5-speed Del Sol Si for sale.  I'd never driven one, so I thought I'd give it a try.<P>I hated it.  First of all, it was gutless.  I thought VTEC Del Sol's were supposed to make 160 hp - this thing was slower than my wife's twin-cam automatic Saturn.  Second of all, it was flexy.  I took the top out and the dashboard shuddered non-stop throughout my test drive, even though the wheels seemed to be balanced properly.  Even K-car convertibles are more solid.  Third of all, the damn thing just up and quit on me while I was sitting at a stoplight idling in neutral.  This, from a six-year-old car with only 60K miles?  It fired right back up, but still...<P>The only positive things I can say are that it had a lot of trunk space, the brakes were really good, and the removable hardtop would be neat if the unibody were more rigid.<P>The dealer wanted $10,900 for it.  Sorry, but for that kind of money I'm thinking 944 Turbo or S2, 94-95 Mustang 5.0, or 5.7 F-body.  Or 3.4 Fiero and LOTS of money left over.<P>I've driven Japanese cars I liked (300ZX, Miata, Maxima), but I have never driven a Honda that made me smile.||||reg||1
Z||000001||dman||08-08-2001||03:27 PM||||Hi Chadman. Wow...that del sol didn't sound too nice.<P>My girlfriend has a del sol. I've only driven it a few times (I prefer to drive my own cars). However I must say that the del sol (at least hers) is an awesome car. Handles great, beautiful interor, etc.<P>Unlike the one you drove, her car has no flexing whatsoever. Her car isn't a vtec and its got about 160000 miles, the throughout bearing needs replacement (it howls) but damn I swear, that little car boogies!!!<P>It loves to wind out. Much faster than my iron duke fiero, maybe even faster than my v6 fieros too.<P>I'm glad you got a chance to try out a del sol. Some people are too close minded to even take one out for a test drive. However I suspect the one you drove was a POS. I wouldn't be surprised if it had been in an accident sometime in the past. Also they're asking way too much for it. I can get a used del sol for less than $6000 any day of the week so that $10k is way overpriced.<P>Like I said earlier, I think the one you drove was a POS. So if you get another chance to test drive a different del sol, go for it. You may have a rather different experience.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||08-08-2001||03:32 PM||||160 HP, ran poorly, stalled at a red light<P>sounds like the previous owner bailed on that car, something seriously wrong with it.<P>anyone else have DelSol flight-time that can give us a test drive report - is this one typical or the exception?||||reg||1
Z||000003||TRiAD||08-08-2001||03:39 PM||||1) Si's are the SOHC VTEC (D16Z6) engine, 125HP.<P>2) This car was obviously NOT maintained. (And I would presume WRECKED.)<P>3) I owned a '95 del Sol Si for nearly a year, after saving it from a goof who did NOT take care of it. It had NONE of the problems you describe. <P>4) How do you know it was an Si? If it was gutless, there was something wrong, or it was a misrepresented S. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||08-08-2001||03:51 PM||||Are you sure it was an SI VTEC? There is a  SOHC SI (125 HP) and the DOHC VTEC model (160 HP). Even the SI should have plenty of pep. I have driven my brothers SI plenty and it is a very quick car and handles great. It sounds like you were just unfortunate to drive a real dog. There is a really nice 97 model here in Saskatoon for sale for 13k Canadian but the damn tings an automatic. Who the heck would buy a four banger auto?!!<P>Here is a link to some specs for the car. Most car magazines clocked the VTEC model 0-60 times in the low 7's and the quarter in the low 15's.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/crx97/delsol/soltech.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/crx97/delsol/soltech.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_11.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1">87 Pontiac Fiero GT<BR>72 Volkswagon Van<P>"Hard work has a future<BR>payoff.  Laziness pays off now"</FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||08-08-2001||04:09 PM||||I don't think the removable roof is a structural part, so if it started flexing after you took it out, it's all in your head. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||08-08-2001||04:20 PM||||Well, it said VTEC on the valve cover, but there was no VTEC badging anywhere else on the car.  It said "Si" on the rear end and was ID'd as an Si on the window sticker.<P>And the flexing was very real.  I took the top out before I drove the car, so I have no idea how it would drive with the top in place -- but it shouldn't make a difference, should it?  <P>If it only made 125 hp, that would explain a lot.  It sure didn't sound mean like the VTEC Integras I've ridden in and lost races to, and I don't think it would run to 60 in less than 9 seconds.  Every V6 Fiero I've ever driven would have handed this Del Sol its a$$.  It was faster than my 88 Coupe, but that's not saying much.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Maybe I'll go drive an RSX.  (I don't think they'll let me drive an S2000 - when the salesman sees my Fiero, he'll know I can't afford it.)<P>Here's the only Honda I ever liked.  Good old Gold - my first bike.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cb3502.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||08-08-2001||04:40 PM||||There was <B>definitely</B> something wrong with that car.  I had a 1995 Civic EX coupe with the 125 horsepower SOHC VTEC motor (same motor as in the Si del Sol) and it easily ran with my wife's 1994 Cavalier with the 140 horsepower 3.1 V6.<P>Man, I miss that car (the Civic, not that POS Chevy)!||||reg||13
Z||000008||TRiAD||08-08-2001||04:56 PM||||Yeah, that was an Si. <BR>I obviously needed REAL help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Nice CB360!||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroKyle||08-08-2001||05:01 PM||||Caviliers a good car. I bit slow. I ran one out in My Fiero drag racing with the 3.1.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||08-08-2001||06:59 PM||||I beat a Cavalier 3.1 z24 in a 89 corolla with the 4Age Mr2 motor...not by much but beat him.<P>As for the del sol , good friend of mine is a honda dealer , they cringe when they come in , notorious for leaks , quirky , and even he says they flex, he had one for a demo , good for the first few 1000kms<P>Del Sol is known as a CRX (3rd gen) everywhere but North America.<P>JM ||||reg||1
