Z||000012||87ECO5||08-09-2001||08:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>Caviliers a good car.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We ordered one from GM (certain color and equipment) and made sure it was a "Wednesday car."  Didn't make a difference.  Car was in the shop 13 times in the 18 short months we owned it.  I've had a bad taste in my mouth for GM stuff ever since.<P>[Knocking on wood] my Fiero has been very good to me but I'd bet she was a pain in the a$$ for the first owner.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000013||firstfiero||08-09-2001||09:19 AM||||     okay here goes...don't care what engine is in the del sol Their is a reason why on the streets their called Del slooooowwwwws. They are cool looking and i like that the roof comes out but they are slow!! <BR>    GM sucks...I won't buy another one after my blazer. done,finished...no more. Their is definitly a reason why they are consistantly ranked as one of the worst cars being made.....nuff said!<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||TRiAD||08-09-2001||09:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>...Their is a reason why on the streets their called Del slooooowwwwws. They are cool looking and i like that the roof comes out but they are slow...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, stock-stock they're quicker than the Fiero GT to 60mph, but that won't matter here, so we'll look at mods...<P>The last del Sol I built had over 320HP <I>at the wheels</I>. It rode on 16" wheels, complete coil-overs, 13" brakes, and had a Supercharged Integra GS-R engine in it, running 10psi of boost. It was a sight to behold, and SLAYED the S2000 and Camaro SS we ran it against...it ran dead even with the NSX we ran it against. This was in a straight line, scratching for traction...none of them could handle it in the corners. <P>FWHP ~ 320<BR>lb/ft torque ~ 300<BR>0-60 ~ 4.8sec<BR>0-100 ~ 12.0<BR>1/4mi ~ 13.5 @ 112MPH<P>Total investment ~ about $15K. <P>Slow? I think not. I'm in the planning stages of another one for another customer right now. It's going to be built more for straight line, and the engine will be an H22A SC, and from our past experience, should make more like 350FWHP. This is in street trim, as in "daily driver". If we can get traction (and not break 1/2 shafts, which some people do over 300HP), it <I>should</I> break into the 12's in street trim. <P>That's faster than a Z06. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||10:01 AM||||Triad you and your magazines......<P>As for it being faster than a GT Fiero.. Don't think so , get all the magazine data you want. I have yet to run across one that is fast. My friends car ran 16.1's in the 1/4 and he has several SCCA solo 2 champion ships under his belt to prove it's not driver related. Again to state...<P>BanditBalzs car ran a 15.2 , and I believe Grinthocks 85 GT was running 15.5's with , both cars stock.<P>Bandit has pulled under 2.0 sec 60 ft times.<P>I'm just waiting for people to post.."Thats impossible ..blah blah blah"<P>Get your car we will see you at the strip<P>And the last z06 I saw at the strip was running 12.4's on street tires. with no mods.<BR>I have AVI video if you would like. I have a video of a chrysler Minivan running 12.3's , doesn't mean it's cool. <P>There is a guy on the Supra list that has a z06 runnin 9's<P>and it looks stock , has a 10" tire , doesn't lift the wheels off the launch..<P>Shaun41178 where are you?? you gave me the link!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChadMan||08-09-2001||11:12 AM||||Sorry - double post<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000017||ChadMan||08-09-2001||11:16 AM||||"I have a video of a chrysler Minivan running 12.3's , doesn't mean it's cool."<P>Man, what a pearl of wisdom that is.  If cool were simply a function of speed, then a Hyundai Tiburon would be cooler than a Porsche 356 or an MGB.<P>TRiAD, I respect your ability to build a fast Honda.  (Really.)  And I respect Honda's ability to make 240 hp from 2 liters (S2000) or 900 hp from 2.65 liters (Champ cars).  But for me, something is missing from the drawing board to the pavement, because I have still never driven a Honda that made me smile and want to own it.||||reg||10
Z||000018||TRiAD||08-09-2001||11:23 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>BanditBalzs car ran a 15.2 , and I believe Grinthocks 85 GT was running 15.5's with , both cars stock. And the last z06 I saw at the strip was running 12.4's on street tires. with no mods.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, but I have GTeched a few Gts to see how close the auto mags were...very close. <BR>There's no way a stock GT will run with a VR6 and an Integra GS-R. There's just no power-weight to support it. <BR>Same with the Z06. 1/4? 13.0. If this guy was running 12.4's stock, he needs to go apply for sainthood.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 1/2 second to 60 is a big deal. <P>We'll probably never agree on this, so let's just agree to disagree. You think stock GTs are 2 seconds to 60 faster than they are, and I have written tests (all within .2 of eachother) to support my own tests.<P>No problem, it's not the end of the world....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RgBSR40Wpe0dBZVWLNqJ!OgcQq654Mh9B*P3DsSLyL7Jq1249HX4l55pKsdufTAOkoEwUubBTWNxu*SB72sRf5PSpElv!BVmIMZ6T1CP4!A/del-Sol-TSC-rear-2.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Slammed Fiero||08-09-2001||12:27 PM||||It's all in good fun..<P>I'm headed to the strip this month for the first time. I will take a GTEC to se how accurate it is..on and off nos.....<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000020||TRiAD||08-09-2001||12:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>It's all in good fun..<P>I'm headed to the strip this month for the first time. I will take a GTEC to se how accurate it is..on and off nos.....<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just keep in mind...GTech doesn't account for <I>reaction time</I>. It begins when you do...not the lights. <P>Have fun!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Black88GT||08-09-2001||02:31 PM||||If you had a Del Sol like you claim, then where are the sponsorships and websites backing it up?  Most of my friends are deep in the import world (sponsored by NOPI amongst others) and they never heard of a Del Sol like the one you described.  The pic you posted is obviously rendered.<P>I'm not saying your lying, but, prove it.  If you did build one like that, more power to you, nothing wrong with fast imports.  <P>Del Sol's are pretty much regarded as girls cars around here.  I never drove one but I raced two and I won by about 7 car lengths, not sure if they were vtec or not.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000022||TRiAD||08-09-2001||02:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>If you had a Del Sol like you claim, then where are the sponsorships and websites backing it up?  ...The pic you posted is obviously rendered.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not everyone has sponsorships. The Integra we did last year was sponsored by<P>* QT<BR>* MMR<BR>* Dunlop<BR>* TRiAD Motorsports (me)<BR>* AEM<BR>* Thermal Research<BR>...and a few more. <P>It was in QT Alloys' booth at Chicago HIN June 2000. (If anyone was there, they/we had a model signong autographs, and the Integra was BLUE with 18"s.)<P>The del Sol I mentioned was built for an out of town customer, as is the one we're planning (with him) now. <P>The pic is a rendered version of what this next one should look like when done. (Well, different sideskirts, but...)<P>Dude, there's MANY Hondas out there running 300HP or so...it's not BIG news, like everyone in the country would know about it. <P>I'll try to get some pics or something, but I don't know what else you want. I really don't have any way to "prove" past projects...Sorry. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Tonker||08-09-2001||04:03 PM||||I've always loved the look of the Del Sols. It was one of the cars that I swore I would own. Love the one in the pic TRiAD.||||reg||14
Z||000024||Black88GT||08-09-2001||06:57 PM||||I understand many Honda's have over 300 hp, no big deal.  However, I have heard that the Integra motor, I believe its the B18A1 or something like that (?) is VERY tough to sway into a CRX, and I think the Del Sol engine comparment is even smaller, so I can't imagine a S/C on it too.  This sounds wild to me, something a lot of people would know about, especially like the guys I know.<P>UPDATE:<BR>Just talked to my friend and cleared things up.  The Integra motor B18C is the one that is VERY tough to swap in, but 91-93 Integra GSR motors aren't too hard.  The U.S. Del Sol VTEC has a B17A which is almost identical to the U.S. Civic Si B16A, 160 hp.  He said with a good driver Del Sols can pull mid-low 15s in the Qtr.<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||firstfiero||08-09-2001||08:40 PM||||    Any car can be made to go fast if you want to supply the cash and the time. As far as a stock car being faster then me your crazy. I have burned more then one del slow. I don't give a crap what numbers in magazines say. I've beaten more then one car that according to the numbers I wasn't supposed to.<BR>    Like I said I like the looks of del sols alot..the one you picture is sweet as hell!<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000026||TRiAD||08-09-2001||10:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I understand many Honda's have over 300 hp, no big deal.  However, I have heard that the Integra motor, I believe its the B18A1 or something like that (?) is VERY tough to sway into a CRX, and I think the Del Sol engine comparment is even smaller, so I can't imagine a S/C on it too.  This sounds wild to me, something a lot of people would know about, especially like the guys I know.<P>UPDATE:<BR>Just talked to my friend and cleared things up.  The Integra motor B18C is the one that is VERY tough to swap in, but 91-93 Integra GSR motors aren't too hard.  The U.S. Del Sol Si with vtec has a B17A which is almost identical to the U.S. Civic Si B16A, 160 hp.  He said with a good driver Del Sols can pull mid-low 15s in the Qtr.<P>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>No offense, but your friend is not well versed in Hondas. <P>The del Sol is the same chassis as all the Integras and Civics of it's series. It is significantly more roomy in the engine bay than the CRX 1 and 2. (The del Sol is technically a CRX III). The swap is plain SIMPLE. It takes 3 hours to 3 days, depending on experience, and is a cookie-cutter plug & play affair. <P>The del Sol Si comes with a SOHC VTEC (D16Z6) engine, while the B18C1 is the easy Integra engine to swap in. <P>It's done every day, and it's no big deal. <P>I like in a Poe-dunk Illinois town with only 15K people, and there are 3 B18C1 powered Civic-variants here. <P>Mid-low 15s (stock) is about right though...if they know how to drive. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Black88GT||08-10-2001||02:25 AM||||According to this site, <A HREF="http://hybrid.honda-perf.org" TARGET=_blank>http://hybrid.honda-perf.org</A>  my friend is right.  The Si Del Sols have the SOHC but the VTEC Del Sols have the B16A2 or B16A3.  <P>Also, that site lists reasons why they dont recommend a B18C integra motor into a 4gen Civic/CRX (aka del sol).<P>B18C <BR>Fabrication issues <BR>The engine mounts have to be moved around for this engine to fit. On top of that only 3 of the 4 B-series mounts can be used and it does compromise the engine's rigidity under heavy torque. Then, there's the issue of cost. <P>Hood clearance problems <BR>The B18C is a taller engine than the stock D-series motor, and the other B-series motors. Hence, custom fabrication results in the engine hanging too low in order for it to clear the hood. This positions the oil pan and exhaust downpipe lower than the front crossmember. <P>Suspension problems <BR>With the low mounted engine the stock suspension's radius rods are about 1/2" from the crank pulley on one side and the transmission housing on the other side. That measurement is at the stock ride height and expect the clearance to be less if the car is lowered. Normal suspension movement in driving will cause the radius rod to hit the pulley or transmission housing. Unless the radius rods are replaced with curved ones, there's no way to protect the engine and suspension from this form of abuse. <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||artherd||08-10-2001||06:40 AM||||Hi Triad, I would like to see some pics of your cars (or any car you've had a hand in, sounds like some impressive work you do) that are NOT photoshoped!!!<P>Please!!!<P>I work in the visual effects industry, but I don't think I can tell a fake still any better than the average joe (so long as joe cares :) but certin look *fake*.<P>How about the real deal for us gearheads?<P>(I wanna see the fiero in your sig come to life, how about it?!?)<P>PS: Del Sols earn their "Del Slow" name, I've driven the Si and the vtech variants, and my 88 Formula (either one) is far and away faster.<P>I do like the cars, and your integra motor swap has gotten me thinking.  Someday.... :)<P>All cars are stock. (ok, my red car's wheels aren't, but that's it driveline wise :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000029||TRiAD||08-10-2001||09:47 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>According to this site, <A HREF="http://hybrid.honda-perf.org" TARGET=_blank>http://hybrid.honda-perf.org</A>  my friend is right.  The Si Del Sols have the SOHC but the VTEC Del Sols have the B16A2 or B16A3.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You said earlier he said the VTEC was a B17 or something...so he wasn't right. <P>Also the del Sol is a <B>5th generation</B> Civic, so he wasn't right again. Go to that forum and see how common a B18C1 is into ANY 5th gen. <P>Other than that, your 4th gen info is right, it's VERY difficult to put the B18 into a 4th gen...but it's still been done.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Art, I'll try to get some pics scanned (if I can get the printer working again...) and get them on the picture server account I just got. I don't have any right now of anything good. Thanks for the compliment, though...<P>L8rs!<P><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||Slammed Fiero||08-10-2001||10:02 AM||||According to a friend who has a Honda dealership. A Del Sol is considered a 3rd Gen Crx.<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
